620 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 383 0 R
/E (This study investigates the extent to which the reduction of open crop straw burning, following Jiangsu's 2009 ban, has contributed to improving air quality and resident health in Baguazhou, an agricultural island in Nanjing, China, over the period of 2010 to 2025. Drawing on official PM2.5 monitoring data, published literature, and a self-conducted survey of long-term Baguazhou residents as supplementary evidence, this paper found a very strong negative correlation with PM2.5 concentrations increasingly declining from 2010 to 2025 and suggests that reduced burning correlates with improved respiratory health in Baguazhou. The paper also reveals that most farmers stopped burning primarily due to external pressure rather than environmental awareness as well as the fact that stealth burning persists, suggesting that while the straw burning ban has been substantially effective in improving air quality and associated health outcomes, the sustainability of this progress depends on strengthening education and practical infrastructure alongside enforcement. )
/Pg 54 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
