706 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 396 0 R
/E (Non-adherence within hypertensive patient populations is a prevalent but complex issue that stems from both constitutional failures and personal decisions. There are three most prominent pillars that contribute to this phenomenon: communicational, socioeconomic and motivational factors. This paper explores the possible application of a growth mindset in resolving motivational issues by increasing the perceived value of treatment and fostering perseverance when faced with medical roadblocks. However, other contributors to non-adherence, such as socioeconomic and communicational barriers, limit the effect of growth mindset application.)
/Pg 67 0 R
/K [1]
>>
